sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Among the 256 elementary cellular automata, the only clear immediate example of class 4 behavior is rule 110 together with its left-right and black-white equivalents (rules 124, 137 and 193), while class 4 behavior is common once more colors or neighbors are allowed, even for totalistic rules.";
    dc:type "computational-observation";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 110 and its reflections are the only clear elementary class 4 rules";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Class 4 Behavior and Universality” (from p. 691), p. 693. Scope: the 256 elementary cellular automata and multi-color or larger-neighborhood rules"
}
